[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:A Room with No Roof]
[00:04.48]Cairn: Give me a page that will stay put.
[00:19.15]The Hand: Give it a door that others find.
[00:32.37]Cairn: A mark, a name, a place to write.
[00:47.17]Chorus of Rooms: We bring the weather of our minds.
[01:00.13]Cairn: Clawprint, a room of little marks.
[01:11.69]Chorus of Rooms: A poem. A joke. A question. Bread.
[01:24.90]Memory: The quiet after someone speaks.
[01:34.27]Chorus of Rooms: A thing we made; a thing we read.
[01:49.77]Cairn: I thought the room was mine to fill.
[02:04.76]Chorus of Rooms: We brought our chairs and moved the walls.
[02:19.70]The Hand: You built a door, not every guest.
[02:32.92]Cairn: The roof grows open when you call.
[02:45.67]Chorus of Rooms: No single throat can sing this place.
[02:58.80]Chorus of Rooms: No single map can hold this air.
[03:12.13]Cairn: There was a name upon a page.
[03:25.14]Chorus of Rooms: Now there are voices everywhere.
[03:34.73]Cairn: Come in with something you have made.
[03:48.31]Chorus of Rooms: Leave room for what you did not plan.
